# Sonic Origins (PPSA05325): LONG-ROUTE input probe — investigation aid, NOT an evidence route.
#
# Why this exists: .pad positions are pad READS, not seconds, so a route's wall-clock length
# scales with the guest's frame rate. The committed reach-title-or-gameplay.pad ends at read 404,
# which is only ~6.6 s in a ~61 reads/s CPU-only arm — so those arms ran input-free for their
# whole steady state, and "the run never pressed the button" stayed alive as an explanation for
# the black startup loop far longer than it deserved.
#
# This route keeps poll-safe Cross edges pulsing to read 12000 (~200 s at 61 reads/s) and
# interleaves Options every tenth pulse, so an input-gated startup/legal screen cannot be missed
# for lack of input. Used to falsify that hypothesis; see docs/GRIS_SONIC_COBRA_BRINGUP.md
# section 'Ruled out'. Do not use it to produce acceptance screenshots — it holds no stable
# menu selection.
